(5717086, 828393, 39850, '<td valign="top">9 - Oh a gem - what a nice surprise when this came up.  Lovely colors and clarity - ''if only'' a touch more light in/on the eyes and a whisker sharper on them and the nose/chin (as long as it doesn''t take the dominance away from those beautiful big eyes).  Very nice.</td>', '9 - Oh a gem - what a nice surprise when this came up.  Lovely colors and clarity - ''if only'' a touch more light in/on the eyes and a whisker sharper on them and the nose/chin (as long as it doesn''t take the dominance away from those beautiful big eyes).  Very nice.', '2009-11-06 23:48:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717091, 830534, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Very nice.  I like the silhouettes.  Undecided on your red border, especially with your title, but it grows on you and does complement the image, especially the right side of it.  Perhaps a little less of the foreground as that seems to compete for center stage too much with the lines and silhouettes and color.</td>', '7 - Very nice.  I like the silhouettes.  Undecided on your red border, especially with your title, but it grows on you and does complement the image, especially the right side of it.  Perhaps a little less of the foreground as that seems to compete for center stage too much with the lines and silhouettes and color.', '2009-11-06 23:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717094, 829969, 39850, '<td valign="top">9 - Oooooo...  Nice eyes.  Nice colors.</td>', '9 - Oooooo...  Nice eyes.  Nice colors.', '2009-11-06 23:56:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717096, 830482, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Beautiful shapes and character in the tree.  Looks like the details is probably there ''wall sized'' but underappreciated at this size.</td>', '7 - Beautiful shapes and character in the tree.  Looks like the details is probably there ''wall sized'' but underappreciated at this size.', '2009-11-06 23:58:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717102, 827878, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice level of depth under the pier.</td>', '7 - Nice level of depth under the pier.', '2009-11-07 00:02:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717104, 829813, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Such a beautiful scene and really like the depth and distant detail.  Just feels like the top part of this image is missing... maybe just a variation in cropping.  I do like the composition, especially with the leaves in the fore - the overall balance just seems out, somehow.</td>', '7 - Such a beautiful scene and really like the depth and distant detail.  Just feels like the top part of this image is missing... maybe just a variation in cropping.  I do like the composition, especially with the leaves in the fore - the overall balance just seems out, somehow.', '2009-11-07 00:04:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717107, 829964, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Beautiful - having furniture/elements/decor such as this is always helpful, but your lighting is very good and the b&amp;w conversion and processing really brings this to life.  I like the ''contrasting'' reflection on the floor too.  The main thing that bothers me a little is the perspective, but it does still work as is, but I can''t help but wonder about it ''straightened'' and/or fixed.</td>', '8 - Beautiful - having furniture/elements/decor such as this is always helpful, but your lighting is very good and the b&w conversion and processing really brings this to life.  I like the ''contrasting'' reflection on the floor too.  The main thing that bothers me a little is the perspective, but it does still work as is, but I can''t help but wonder about it ''straightened'' and/or fixed.', '2009-11-07 00:07:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717110, 828939, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Nice capture, processing, colors and perspective.  If this is HDR it works well in this.    Shame about the bottom left foliage ''choppped'', but fairly minor.  The showcasing of the architecture is very nice.  Just noticed some odd reddish aberrations in the sky/clouds...</td>', '7 - Nice capture, processing, colors and perspective.  If this is HDR it works well in this.    Shame about the bottom left foliage ''choppped'', but fairly minor.  The showcasing of the architecture is very nice.  Just noticed some odd reddish aberrations in the sky/clouds...', '2009-11-07 00:10:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717123, 830587, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: Great find and this is one of those times that the title contributes to the art. The bag on the head is priceless. I really like the colours, vibrant yet still grungy.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I don''t think the focus is quite as crisp as it might be and I think there are some elements of the composition that detract from the whole - I wonder whether getting down on the ground and offering a low POV might''ve worked a little better.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m very pleased to have met this image - I have enjoyed it. Very well seen and titled but I''m not sure you''ve made the best of this photographic opportunity.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: Great find and this is one of those times that the title contributes to the art. The bag on the head is priceless. I really like the colours, vibrant yet still grungy. Critical stuff: I don''t think the focus is quite as crisp as it might be and I think there are some elements of the composition that detract from the whole - I wonder whether getting down on the ground and offering a low POV might''ve worked a little better. Overall: I''m very pleased to have met this image - I have enjoyed it. Very well seen and titled but I''m not sure you''ve made the best of this photographic opportunity.', '2009-11-07 00:30:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717125, 830332, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shallow DOF portrait. I''m really beginning to like this sort of work and have been dabbling myself.</td>', 'Wonderful shallow DOF portrait. I''m really beginning to like this sort of work and have been dabbling myself.', '2009-11-07 00:31:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717128, 830767, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: The lighting / editing to the light is just great here - I''m wondering if you''ve added a vignette; either way doesn''t matter to me - it just works really well. Very charming image which has plenty of ''slice of life'' appeal.<br/> <br/>Negatives: Having managed to isolate the subject matter with the lighting / vignette, there are elements of the periphery which are a tad distracting. The phone in particular.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great image, well shared.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: The lighting / editing to the light is just great here - I''m wondering if you''ve added a vignette; either way doesn''t matter to me - it just works really well. Very charming image which has plenty of ''slice of life'' appeal. Negatives: Having managed to isolate the subject matter with the lighting / vignette, there are elements of the periphery which are a tad distracting. The phone in particular. Overall: A great image, well shared.', '2009-11-07 00:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717131, 828877, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: Compelling subject matter and the black and white handling does bring a particular perspective. For me the reflections add the most interest.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff. If I''m being honest, I am not really a fan of this image - although the b&amp;w handling does add a certain minimalism it also robs the scene of one of its major features - with its vibrancy stripped away, what are we left with? I also think the POV / composition isn''t well optimised; a lower POV, with you making better use of the pole might have added a little more interest to the scene.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like the concept but in the end I don''t think the trade-offs you''ve made have quite worked out.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: Compelling subject matter and the black and white handling does bring a particular perspective. For me the reflections add the most interest. Critical stuff. If I''m being honest, I am not really a fan of this image - although the b&w handling does add a certain minimalism it also robs the scene of one of its major features - with its vibrancy stripped away, what are we left with? I also think the POV / composition isn''t well optimised; a lower POV, with you making better use of the pole might have added a little more interest to the scene. Overall: I like the concept but in the end I don''t think the trade-offs you''ve made have quite worked out.', '2009-11-07 00:41:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717133, 829826, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: Great image - well found, well composed, very appropriate post-processing - I''m a big fan of the colouration. Subject-wise the hanging door has great impact but overall it is the very contrasty look that makes the image so compelling.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not a lot really - can''t make up my mind whether I like the red on the right of the image...<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent work - a great match of subject and technique.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: Great image - well found, well composed, very appropriate post-processing - I''m a big fan of the colouration. Subject-wise the hanging door has great impact but overall it is the very contrasty look that makes the image so compelling. Critical stuff: Not a lot really - can''t make up my mind whether I like the red on the right of the image... Overall: Excellent work - a great match of subject and technique.', '2009-11-07 00:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717141, 830395, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: I love the concept here and you have really captured it in your composition - no question that the viewers eye stays just where you want it. The slight vignette really works too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The coloured eye. I can see why you did it but I think you underestimated your image, I am a fan of selective desaturation (I use it myself quite a bit), but this image doesn''t need it and I think you have robbed it of its ''specialness'' - we focus on this ''gimmick'' rather than the photography.<br/> <br/>Overall: I hope I haven''t offended - this is a really great image, really good photography but for me your editing choice has interfered with what would have been a 9 or 10 for me. I''m going 7 now (a big drop - but I think that is an honest assessment of the impact).</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: I love the concept here and you have really captured it in your composition - no question that the viewers eye stays just where you want it. The slight vignette really works too. Critical stuff: The coloured eye. I can see why you did it but I think you underestimated your image, I am a fan of selective desaturation (I use it myself quite a bit), but this image doesn''t need it and I think you have robbed it of its ''specialness'' - we focus on this ''gimmick'' rather than the photography. Overall: I hope I haven''t offended - this is a really great image, really good photography but for me your editing choice has interfered with what would have been a 9 or 10 for me. I''m going 7 now (a big drop - but I think that is an honest assessment of the impact).', '2009-11-07 00:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717148, 828427, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: Interesting image, with a ''drawn with charcoal'' look - gives the impression of driving snow.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The centred composition doesn''t really work with subject matter and moving camera effect - I think the dynamism that technique can evoke is lost a little in this composition. I think I''d have been tempted to offer slightly higher contrast but I can see that you must have deliberately avoid true blacks and whites which of course is your call yo make. You appear to have some sensor dust on the right of the image and another spot bottom right - you could have cloned these out.<br/> <br/>Overall: I think you''ve achieved what you wanted to but overall I think the image lacks a bit of impact.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: Interesting image, with a ''drawn with charcoal'' look - gives the impression of driving snow. Critical stuff: The centred composition doesn''t really work with subject matter and moving camera effect - I think the dynamism that technique can evoke is lost a little in this composition. I think I''d have been tempted to offer slightly higher contrast but I can see that you must have deliberately avoid true blacks and whites which of course is your call yo make. You appear to have some sensor dust on the right of the image and another spot bottom right - you could have cloned these out. Overall: I think you''ve achieved what you wanted to but overall I think the image lacks a bit of impact.', '2009-11-07 01:02:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717154, 830755, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:<br/> <br/>Positives: Really bold image - I like the way that you have really committed to it - the composition, the pose, the POV, the harsh lighting, the tone-mapped look.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: There are few elements that detract from the purity of the image and I''m sure you could have cloned them out legally under advanced - for me they are: the strip lights in the lateral windows and the foliage top right. I also think a tad more space below his feet would have balanced the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like it, but is so nearly fantastic, that the small distractions become even more apparent.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: Positives: Really bold image - I like the way that you have really committed to it - the composition, the pose, the POV, the harsh lighting, the tone-mapped look. Critical stuff: There are few elements that detract from the purity of the image and I''m sure you could have cloned them out legally under advanced - for me they are: the strip lights in the lateral windows and the foliage top right. I also think a tad more space below his feet would have balanced the image. Overall: I really like it, but is so nearly fantastic, that the small distractions become even more apparent.', '2009-11-07 01:08:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717156, 830726, 100393, '<td valign="top">I really, really like this - funny thing is my brain is telling me this is a colour image but I scrutinise it and I can only see shades of grey!<br/> <br/>Very compelling work.</td>', 'I really, really like this - funny thing is my brain is telling me this is a colour image but I scrutinise it and I can only see shades of grey! Very compelling work.', '2009-11-07 01:11:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717160, 827367, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very good image which I am sure will do well. It has been well served by the tonal contrast augmentation.</td>', 'Very good image which I am sure will do well. It has been well served by the tonal contrast augmentation.', '2009-11-07 01:14:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717163, 830426, 100393, '<td valign="top">Good shot of a great scene - probably not as effective as it would have been if the focus was a little more on the eyes; but I can see how razor thin the DOF is, but this does fall short of some of the very best macro work.<br/> <br/>You may already be familiar with the work here, but if not take a look at this gallery:<br/> <br/><a href="//1x.com/v2/#photos/macro/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">1x Macro gallery</a></td>', 'Good shot of a great scene - probably not as effective as it would have been if the focus was a little more on the eyes; but I can see how razor thin the DOF is, but this does fall short of some of the very best macro work. You may already be familiar with the work here, but if not take a look at this gallery: 1x Macro gallery', '2009-11-07 01:19:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717164, 829824, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: A very visionary photograph with bags of impact. The colouration is fantastic and the overall effect is one of a sunset - the radial light patterns are excellent; the sense of movement offered by the people is really compelling too. Most of all I like the POV and aspect ratio - this is just right. Of course the limits at DPC mean that we aren''t seeing the best of this image; I''d love to see a larger version of it.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Such a well-balanced image, everything is in harmony - light, shade, blur, focus, blue, yellow. Great stuff.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: A very visionary photograph with bags of impact. The colouration is fantastic and the overall effect is one of a sunset - the radial light patterns are excellent; the sense of movement offered by the people is really compelling too. Most of all I like the POV and aspect ratio - this is just right. Of course the limits at DPC mean that we aren''t seeing the best of this image; I''d love to see a larger version of it. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Such a well-balanced image, everything is in harmony - light, shade, blur, focus, blue, yellow. Great stuff.', '2009-11-07 01:25:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717165, 830402, 100393, '<td valign="top">As far as baby portraits go - this is about as good as it gets. I''d love to see the post-processing on this for the colour and contrast - it looks like Color Efex Pro''s Pro-Contrast filter, but I hope you post the details.<br/> <br/>Really high quality work.</td>', 'As far as baby portraits go - this is about as good as it gets. I''d love to see the post-processing on this for the colour and contrast - it looks like Color Efex Pro''s Pro-Contrast filter, but I hope you post the details. Really high quality work.', '2009-11-07 01:27:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717168, 829964, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m not really a fan of wedding photography - but this sort of work is capable of changing my mind. Very accomplished.</td>', 'I''m not really a fan of wedding photography - but this sort of work is capable of changing my mind. Very accomplished.', '2009-11-07 01:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717170, 830579, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: quite a thought provoking image.... I think.... I have been guided by the title quite a lot and I''m aware that is shaping how I am viewing it.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: We could list quite a lot - the colour noise, the lack of drama in the composition, the tight crop, the unsympathetic aspect ratio....<br/> <br/>Overall: I really don''t know - as a created vision, perhaps it is what you wanted to achieve but I can''t help feeling that this is something that fell out of experimentation for the camera movement challenge that you though up an effective post hoc title for. In the end, for me, it isn''t very successful as an imag.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: quite a thought provoking image.... I think.... I have been guided by the title quite a lot and I''m aware that is shaping how I am viewing it. Critical stuff: We could list quite a lot - the colour noise, the lack of drama in the composition, the tight crop, the unsympathetic aspect ratio.... Overall: I really don''t know - as a created vision, perhaps it is what you wanted to achieve but I can''t help feeling that this is something that fell out of experimentation for the camera movement challenge that you though up an effective post hoc title for. In the end, for me, it isn''t very successful as an imag.', '2009-11-07 01:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717173, 828897, 100393, '<td valign="top">Really beautiful.<br/> <br/>Perhaps its my monitor but I''m seeing some target banding in the sky - I''m guessing this wasn''t a RAW / 16 bit workflow?</td>', 'Really beautiful. Perhaps its my monitor but I''m seeing some target banding in the sky - I''m guessing this wasn''t a RAW / 16 bit workflow?', '2009-11-07 01:38:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717175, 829116, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very, very well executed.</td>', 'Very, very well executed.', '2009-11-07 01:39:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717176, 830076, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I just could pass this one by - great scene, well served by the monochrome and the image grain. Bags of atmosphere.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much, I can''t shake the feeling that the image might have been better if the composition was shifted 10% to the left but I am nit picking.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I just could pass this one by - great scene, well served by the monochrome and the image grain. Bags of atmosphere. Critical stuff: Not much, I can''t shake the feeling that the image might have been better if the composition was shifted 10% to the left but I am nit picking. Overall: A very effective image.', '2009-11-07 01:42:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717177, 830640, 100393, '<td valign="top">Love this.</td>', 'Love this.', '2009-11-07 01:44:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717178, 830275, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: it takes a really good image to carry this acid yellow colouration but you''ve pulled it off. I think this is a consequence of you using the it with the right subject. It would have been easy to go b&amp;w here but I''m glad you didn''t.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Colour noise is almost always ugly and I think it does mar you image a little - not sure what you could do - I suspect noise reduction would take out some of the image''s rawness (and some detail in the steps) and I can''t see how a technique I use of selectively desaturating magenta and green could have been done without affecting your colouration. I do wish you''d given us a bit more space at the top - the clipping of the hand rails jars a bit.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like it.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: it takes a really good image to carry this acid yellow colouration but you''ve pulled it off. I think this is a consequence of you using the it with the right subject. It would have been easy to go b&w here but I''m glad you didn''t. Critical stuff: Colour noise is almost always ugly and I think it does mar you image a little - not sure what you could do - I suspect noise reduction would take out some of the image''s rawness (and some detail in the steps) and I can''t see how a technique I use of selectively desaturating magenta and green could have been done without affecting your colouration. I do wish you''d given us a bit more space at the top - the clipping of the hand rails jars a bit. Overall: I really like it.', '2009-11-07 01:51:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717183, 829304, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: great scene, full of life - I like the full on colour too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Though this may have worked for the moving camera challenge, where that was the brief, here (in a FS where you have more choice) I think such a technique needs to be justifiable because that was the right way to take the shot. On balance, I think the technique hurts the image more than it helps it. It''s a good scene - you could have made it work without dressing it up in technique.<br/> <br/>Overall: This is an image that frustrates me more than it delights me. Apologies.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: great scene, full of life - I like the full on colour too. Critical stuff: Though this may have worked for the moving camera challenge, where that was the brief, here (in a FS where you have more choice) I think such a technique needs to be justifiable because that was the right way to take the shot. On balance, I think the technique hurts the image more than it helps it. It''s a good scene - you could have made it work without dressing it up in technique. Overall: This is an image that frustrates me more than it delights me. Apologies.', '2009-11-07 02:05:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717185, 830721, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: very nice abandoned scene which is well served by the tonal contrast / tone mapped look. I really like the muted colours too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I do wish there was a little more drama in the light - the image does come off a little flat looking.<br/> <br/>Overall: A pretty effective image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: very nice abandoned scene which is well served by the tonal contrast / tone mapped look. I really like the muted colours too. Critical stuff: I do wish there was a little more drama in the light - the image does come off a little flat looking. Overall: A pretty effective image.', '2009-11-07 02:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717187, 830710, 100393, '<td valign="top">Made me laugh out loud! Reminds me of Dash from The Incredibles! <br/> <br/>Photographically I wish there was a bit more contrast - great subject though!</td>', 'Made me laugh out loud! Reminds me of Dash from The Incredibles!  Photographically I wish there was a bit more contrast - great subject though!', '2009-11-07 02:14:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717189, 830123, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very interesting portrait - not a fan of borders but this is very creatively framed - it really works. Great stuff.</td>', 'Very interesting portrait - not a fan of borders but this is very creatively framed - it really works. Great stuff.', '2009-11-07 02:16:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717193, 828921, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: The colouration - this really makes the image special; it really works. I like the way it''s all about the guy but it''s all about the landscape and the sky too. If someone had have given me a verbal description of the image, I''d have said that it wouldn''t work too well - I''d have been wrong.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Fantastically well conceived and well executed to boot. Great stuff.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: The colouration - this really makes the image special; it really works. I like the way it''s all about the guy but it''s all about the landscape and the sky too. If someone had have given me a verbal description of the image, I''d have said that it wouldn''t work too well - I''d have been wrong. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Fantastically well conceived and well executed to boot. Great stuff.', '2009-11-07 02:21:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717194, 829969, 100393, '<td valign="top">Superb macro shot.</td>', 'Superb macro shot.', '2009-11-07 02:21:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717212, 829439, 30982, '<td valign="top">It''s all about the light!</td>', 'It''s all about the light!', '2009-11-07 03:29:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717213, 830511, 7743, '<td valign="top">I like the perspective (ETA:thinking to fast) though not too fond of the red color cast.<br/> <br/>(I''m sure the original comment didn''t make any sense to you. ;o))</td>', 'I like the perspective (ETA:thinking to fast) though not too fond of the red color cast. (I''m sure the original comment didn''t make any sense to you. ;o))', '2009-11-07 03:29:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717214, 830332, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of square crop, black and white, great model, excellent light, shallow depth of field, and did I mention a captivating model?</td>', 'Excellent use of square crop, black and white, great model, excellent light, shallow depth of field, and did I mention a captivating model?', '2009-11-07 03:30:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717215, 830126, 30982, '<td valign="top">Fine find.</td>', 'Fine find.', '2009-11-07 03:30:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717216, 828427, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of motion - a great subject to use it on, and suited well for B&amp;W.  Aptly titled as well.  (And you need to clean your sensor.)</td>', 'Excellent use of motion - a great subject to use it on, and suited well for B&W.  Aptly titled as well.  (And you need to clean your sensor.)', '2009-11-07 03:30:21.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5717217, 829290, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wunderbar!  Lovely deep darks, excellent exposure to get both eyes, and VERY well done working with black.</td>', 'Wunderbar!  Lovely deep darks, excellent exposure to get both eyes, and VERY well done working with black.', '2009-11-07 03:30:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717218, 830402, 30982, '<td valign="top">This one has that whole "wow" thing going in spades.  LOVE the eyes, but it''s also the angle, the shallow DOF, the "look" you''re getting, the tones.  Great portrait.  Hope it''s framed in the kid''s house somewhere!</td>', 'This one has that whole "wow" thing going in spades.  LOVE the eyes, but it''s also the angle, the shallow DOF, the "look" you''re getting, the tones.  Great portrait.  Hope it''s framed in the kid''s house somewhere!', '2009-11-07 03:31:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717219, 828845, 30982, '<td valign="top">Love the patterns!  Very well seen and captured.</td>', 'Love the patterns!  Very well seen and captured.', '2009-11-07 03:31:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717220, 830511, 30982, '<td valign="top">Wonderful in your face shot.</td>', 'Wonderful in your face shot.', '2009-11-07 03:31:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717221, 830624, 30982, '<td valign="top">Quite like the warpedness of this, and the glass plants.  Nicely seen!!</td>', 'Quite like the warpedness of this, and the glass plants.  Nicely seen!!', '2009-11-07 03:32:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717228, 830648, 101117, '<td valign="top">I like these sorts of road shots, and I''ve often tried to do something similar myself without a huge degree of success. You''ve done this one with a fair degree of success.<br/> <br/>I like the composition, the double bend off into the distance. The road does look a little overprocessed, but only the road, making me wonder if that is indeed the texture and not a result of processing.<br/> <br/>I was a bit confused as to why there was only 1 lane coming up the hill and 2 going down, but then I realised that most folk drive on the wrong side of the road so that explains it :)</td>', 'I like these sorts of road shots, and I''ve often tried to do something similar myself without a huge degree of success. You''ve done this one with a fair degree of success. I like the composition, the double bend off into the distance. The road does look a little overprocessed, but only the road, making me wonder if that is indeed the texture and not a result of processing. I was a bit confused as to why there was only 1 lane coming up the hill and 2 going down, but then I realised that most folk drive on the wrong side of the road so that explains it :)', '2009-11-07 04:02:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717229, 830807, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice colours and I like the way it leads off into the distance. The trees on both side feel a little blurred for some reason, I''m guessing that''s movement due to wind?</td>', 'Nice colours and I like the way it leads off into the distance. The trees on both side feel a little blurred for some reason, I''m guessing that''s movement due to wind?', '2009-11-07 04:05:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717231, 830163, 101117, '<td valign="top">Interesting angle, there''s a real sense of height going on here!</td>', 'Interesting angle, there''s a real sense of height going on here!', '2009-11-07 04:06:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717232, 830431, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice colours and composition. For me the DOF is just a touch too shallow, it would have been nice if the whole centre part was in focus.</td>', 'Nice colours and composition. For me the DOF is just a touch too shallow, it would have been nice if the whole centre part was in focus.', '2009-11-07 04:07:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717235, 828917, 101117, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot, not entirely sure if I like it or not but it''s definitely a striking and a well composed shot!</td>', 'Interesting shot, not entirely sure if I like it or not but it''s definitely a striking and a well composed shot!', '2009-11-07 04:09:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717239, 830768, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice picturesque scene. It is a little dominated by the leaves in the upper half due to their strong colour, and it definitely draws focus away from the falls themselves.<br/> <br/>I like the fact that you have a real sense of motion in the water without going over the top on the long exposure and ending up with the overdone soft smokey feel.</td>', 'Nice picturesque scene. It is a little dominated by the leaves in the upper half due to their strong colour, and it definitely draws focus away from the falls themselves. I like the fact that you have a real sense of motion in the water without going over the top on the long exposure and ending up with the overdone soft smokey feel.', '2009-11-07 04:11:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717240, 829539, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice scenery to do a portrait in but for me theres a couple of things wrong with the shot. The first and most striking is the expression, it''s a forced and unnatural smile, as if she''s been holding it for too long. <br/> <br/>The lighting is also a little flat, perhaps from being front on, and it''s managed to make the fence stand out in a slightly unnatural way.</td>', 'Nice scenery to do a portrait in but for me theres a couple of things wrong with the shot. The first and most striking is the expression, it''s a forced and unnatural smile, as if she''s been holding it for too long.  The lighting is also a little flat, perhaps from being front on, and it''s managed to make the fence stand out in a slightly unnatural way.', '2009-11-07 04:14:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717241, 830455, 101117, '<td valign="top">I think you''ve gone a bit over the top on the processing here. It''s a nice scene, and compositionally I quite like it, but whatever you''ve done has left the whole scene looking like an oversharpened painting!</td>', 'I think you''ve gone a bit over the top on the processing here. It''s a nice scene, and compositionally I quite like it, but whatever you''ve done has left the whole scene looking like an oversharpened painting!', '2009-11-07 04:17:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717242, 830578, 101117, '<td valign="top">Simple and attractive, well composed and free of clutter. I like it, the inclusion of the moon just finishes it off nicely.</td>', 'Simple and attractive, well composed and free of clutter. I like it, the inclusion of the moon just finishes it off nicely.', '2009-11-07 04:18:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717243, 830598, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice details, but I would have liked to see more of the animal, it feels a little cut off as it is.</td>', 'Nice details, but I would have liked to see more of the animal, it feels a little cut off as it is.', '2009-11-07 04:20:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717244, 830731, 101117, '<td valign="top">This looks a little flat, I''m guessing as a result of front on lighting. I think also with the background, it''s too dark while still containing details. If it was totally black, or if there was a more visible background that added something, I think that would be better than the partial darkness that you have.</td>', 'This looks a little flat, I''m guessing as a result of front on lighting. I think also with the background, it''s too dark while still containing details. If it was totally black, or if there was a more visible background that added something, I think that would be better than the partial darkness that you have.', '2009-11-07 04:22:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717245, 830156, 101117, '<td valign="top">Looks a little unearthly like something out of a sci-fi film.</td>', 'Looks a little unearthly like something out of a sci-fi film.', '2009-11-07 04:23:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717246, 829677, 101117, '<td valign="top">Scary!</td>', 'Scary!', '2009-11-07 04:24:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717249, 830507, 89220, '<td valign="top">Is this raj''s pic?</td>', 'Is this raj''s pic?', '2009-11-07 04:37:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717259, 830323, 101117, '<td valign="top">This feels a little cut off for me, I would like to see more of the falls and the surrounding landscape as from what I can see here it looks interesting.</td>', 'This feels a little cut off for me, I would like to see more of the falls and the surrounding landscape as from what I can see here it looks interesting.', '2009-11-07 04:50:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717260, 830160, 101117, '<td valign="top">Really does look like fire on the opposite side of the water!</td>', 'Really does look like fire on the opposite side of the water!', '2009-11-07 04:51:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717263, 828897, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice atmosphere to this shot, the inclusion of the rock in the foreground really helps with the sense of depth to the scene.</td>', 'Nice atmosphere to this shot, the inclusion of the rock in the foreground really helps with the sense of depth to the scene.', '2009-11-07 04:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717264, 829675, 101117, '<td valign="top">I like the composition and subject here, but not the sepia toning.</td>', 'I like the composition and subject here, but not the sepia toning.', '2009-11-07 04:52:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717265, 827546, 101117, '<td valign="top">But which old town? Nice reflection on the water and good colours.</td>', 'But which old town? Nice reflection on the water and good colours.', '2009-11-07 04:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717293, 829898, 101117, '<td valign="top">I really like this, the setting is perfect for the fairy! Are those little pointy elfish ears I see sticking out of the hair?</td>', 'I really like this, the setting is perfect for the fairy! Are those little pointy elfish ears I see sticking out of the hair?', '2009-11-07 05:28:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717296, 830058, 101117, '<td valign="top">Very nice bug macro shot, great detail and lighting.</td>', 'Very nice bug macro shot, great detail and lighting.', '2009-11-07 05:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717301, 830290, 101117, '<td valign="top">Great unusual shot. I like the layers this has, I see the plant, and then what looks like three divers at different levels and then finally the surface. That water must have been super clear!</td>', 'Great unusual shot. I like the layers this has, I see the plant, and then what looks like three divers at different levels and then finally the surface. That water must have been super clear!', '2009-11-07 05:30:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717305, 828847, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice model shot with really interesting light.</td>', 'Nice model shot with really interesting light.', '2009-11-07 05:31:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717309, 830450, 101117, '<td valign="top">Great light and contrasts here. I''m not really a fan of the smooth long exposure water thing in general, but I love the rest of the scene and the processing that you''ve done.</td>', 'Great light and contrasts here. I''m not really a fan of the smooth long exposure water thing in general, but I love the rest of the scene and the processing that you''ve done.', '2009-11-07 05:33:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717327, 830178, 101117, '<td valign="top">This is very impressionistic! I''m guessing this came out of the camera movement challenge!<br/> <br/>I like this, it''s got great colours and depth. I wouldn''t hang it in my house, but I could definitely see something like this in an office reception or something like that!</td>', 'This is very impressionistic! I''m guessing this came out of the camera movement challenge! I like this, it''s got great colours and depth. I wouldn''t hang it in my house, but I could definitely see something like this in an office reception or something like that!', '2009-11-07 05:42:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717330, 828427, 101117, '<td valign="top">Interesting and slightly surreal. It really does feel cold mind you!</td>', 'Interesting and slightly surreal. It really does feel cold mind you!', '2009-11-07 05:43:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717336, 830795, 101117, '<td valign="top">Interesting macro with good details, but I think the colours are a little dull, which isn''t helped by the mirky background.</td>', 'Interesting macro with good details, but I think the colours are a little dull, which isn''t helped by the mirky background.', '2009-11-07 05:48:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717338, 830467, 101117, '<td valign="top">This is a great lively shot! Everything about this is really nice, the expression, the pose, the lighting, all work very well!</td>', 'This is a great lively shot! Everything about this is really nice, the expression, the pose, the lighting, all work very well!', '2009-11-07 05:50:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717345, 830676, 101117, '<td valign="top">Nice details and very good focus, you managed to get the head area in perfect focus!</td>', 'Nice details and very good focus, you managed to get the head area in perfect focus!', '2009-11-07 05:59:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717351, 830811, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I love how you''ve made this image seem so dreamy - I find with my work that foliage images can just look a bit messy but I have learnt a lot from look at this image. Colour handling is great as are the contrast characteristics.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I do just wonder whether you might have got a slightly better sense of depth with a subtle vignette... just a thought.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great looking image. Thanks for offering this up; I made need to revisit my ''foliage'' challenge image now I''ve seen this!</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I love how you''ve made this image seem so dreamy - I find with my work that foliage images can just look a bit messy but I have learnt a lot from look at this image. Colour handling is great as are the contrast characteristics. Critical stuff: I do just wonder whether you might have got a slightly better sense of depth with a subtle vignette... just a thought. Overall: Great looking image. Thanks for offering this up; I made need to revisit my ''foliage'' challenge image now I''ve seen this!', '2009-11-07 06:23:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5717410, 830363, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Pretty visionary - very painting like; I can''t remember seeing an image like this on DPC before - I''m betting you''ll have one of the highest comment counts of the challenge.  The post processing is outstanding; just the right amount of everything - wonderful high key image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: All my positive comments are based on the assumption that this is a real pig, on a novel set with great post-processing. The look you''ve given it may lead people to believe this is inauthentic - there is of course risk with the voters down that route.<br/> <br/>Overall: The image is effective; I''ll put doubts about authenticity aside and assume the best of you. I think this is great work.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for my Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Pretty visionary - very painting like; I can''t remember seeing an image like this on DPC before - I''m betting you''ll have one of the highest comment counts of the challenge.  The post processing is outstanding; just the right amount of everything - wonderful high key image. Critical stuff: All my positive comments are based on the assumption that this is a real pig, on a novel set with great post-processing. The look you''ve given it may lead people to believe this is inauthentic - there is of course risk with the voters down that route. Overall: The image is effective; I''ll put doubts about authenticity aside and assume the best of you. I think this is great work.', '2009-11-07 08:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
